# Files in this package that stow should NOT link into $HOME.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file *replaces* stow's built-in ignore list rather than
# extending it, so the built-in defaults are reproduced verbatim below.
# Dropping \.git in particular would make stow link ~/.git to this repo's
# git directory and turn $HOME into a git working tree.
#
# Patterns are Perl regexes. A pattern with no "/" is matched against each
# path segment, fully anchored; one containing "/" is matched against the
# path relative to the package root. Hence \.git matches only ".git", not
# ".git_hidden_message" -- that one needs its own entry.

# --- stow's built-in defaults (do not drop) ---
RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore

.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

# --- specific to this package ---
# Provisioning script, run from the repo; not a dotfile.
^/install_dev_tools\.sh
^/\.git_hidden_message
